<pdd-reason>The pop-up cards must appear over the live Twitch stream while claw-dj plays autonomously on the Mac mini, without changing the mix runner, and OBS must be able to show them from any machine on the network.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {"name": "audible_deck", "signature": "audible_deck(mixxx, decks: tuple[int, ...] = (1, 2, 3, 4)) -> int | None"},
      {"name": "identify_by_duration", "signature": "identify_by_duration(duration_s: float, candidates: list[dict], tolerance_s: float = 0.6, bpm: float | None = None) -> dict | None"},
      {"name": "plan_candidates", "signature": "plan_candidates(index_path: Path | None = None, plans_dir: Path | None = None, *, probe: bool = True) -> list[dict]"},
      {"name": "make_server", "signature": "make_server(scheduler: Scheduler, now_playing, *, host: str = '0.0.0.0', port: int = 8765) -> ThreadingHTTPServer"}
    ],
    "classes": [
      {"name": "NowPlaying", "signature": "NowPlaying(*, mixxx_port: int | None = None, now_file: Path | None = None, candidates: list[dict] | None = None, cache_s: float = 2.0)", "methods": ["current() -> tuple[str | None, str | None]"]}
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

% Goal

Serve `brain.popups` cards as a transparent browser-source overlay for OBS / Twitch, aware of the song claw-dj is playing in Mixxx (`user_stories/story__while_the_mix_plays_pop_ups_show_music_facts_and_my_commentary.md`).

% Requirements

1. `audible_deck(mixxx)` returns the playing, loaded deck with the largest effective level. The level is channel volume times crossfader gain: decks 1 and 3 sit on the left, 2 and 4 on the right; the far side fades linearly across the crossfader. It returns None when nothing audible is playing. It only reads Mixxx controls.
2. `identify_by_duration(duration, candidates, bpm=None)`: a candidate (`artist`, `title`, `duration`, optional `tol`, optional `bpm`) matches when its duration is within its own `tol`, else within `tolerance_s`.
   - One match: return it.
   - Several: keep only those whose `bpm` equals the deck's analyzed `file_bpm` within 2%, allowing half- and double-time readings. Return the one left, if exactly one.
   - Otherwise return None (no guessing).
3. `plan_candidates()` returns the active plan's tracks (`brain/data/plans/active.json` -> `<slug>/mix_plan.json`) with durations and BPM, or an empty list when the plan is missing.
   - Durations: read exactly from the audio files with ffprobe, in parallel, once (`tol` 0.15 s). Fall back to the library index's coarser durations (`tol` 0.6 s) when a file can't be read. The library rounds to about half a second, so durations alone collide (measured 2026-10-12: 141 of 203 tracks within 0.6 s of another).
4. `NowPlaying.current()`:
   - With `now_file` (JSON `{"artist", "title"}`): returns its content, so it works without Mixxx.
   - Otherwise: reads Mixxx through `hands.mixxx_control` and identifies the audible deck's `duration` (and `file_bpm` for ties) against the candidates.
   - Results are cached for `cache_s`.
   - Any connection or parse error gives `(None, None)`, never an exception. The overlay must never disturb the mix.
5. `make_server` serves:
   - `GET /overlay`: the HTML page;
   - `GET /card`: JSON `{"serial", "card", "show_s"}`. It ticks the scheduler with the current song and returns the active card while it is within its `show_s` window, else null. `serial` increments with each new card;
   - `GET /health`: `{"ok": true}`;
   - anything else: 404.

   It binds `host` (default all interfaces, so OBS on another machine can reach it). Logging is quiet.
6. The page:
   - Background: fully transparent.
   - Polling: polls `/card` about once a second; a new serial shows a VH1-style rounded bubble with large text that pops in, stays `show_s`, then pops out, in one of several safe on-screen positions.
   - Commentary: a small subtle EY-style monogram badge with the card's initials. A quote is shown in quotation marks; a distilled card shows a small "in brief" label; a progression shows "i/n".
   - Facts: no badge.
   - `?scale=` scales the bubble.
7. CLI: `python -m hands.popup_overlay [--host H] [--port P] [--interval S] [--show S] [--commentary-every N] [--verified-only] [--now-file PATH] [--facts PATH] [--commentary DIR]`. It prints the overlay URL to add as an OBS Browser Source.
8. No writes to Mixxx, no audio, no network beyond the local HTTP server and the local Mixxx control port.

% Verification

- `uv run python -m unittest tests/test_popup_overlay.py` with a fake Mixxx and a server on an ephemeral port. No live Mixxx.
- Cover:
  - audible-deck choice with the crossfader;
  - unique-duration identification and ambiguity giving None;
  - now-file mode;
  - errors giving `(None, None)`;
  - `/card`, `/overlay` and `/health` responses, and 404 for anything else;
  - EY metadata reaching the JSON for commentary and not for facts.
